      lead: 'Sholo Guti ("sixteen pieces" in Bengali) is an old two-player village game played on lines drawn on the ground, with pebbles or seeds as pieces. Each side has 16 pieces and captures by jumping over the other side\'s pieces. Here are the full rules in simple words.',
      needH: 'What you need',
